  "jd_text": "### **HR Assistant \u2014 Prime Focus Group (Prime AC)**\n\n**Location:** Dubai, UAE (on-site) \u00b7 **Reports to:** HR Manager \u00b7 **Function:** Human Resources \u00b7 **Level:** Assistant / junior (this is a hands-on admin seat, not a supervisory role)\n\n**Role summary**  \n Support the full employee lifecycle for a UAE HVAC/ductwork manufacturing operation spanning a factory workforce and office staff \u2014 visa and labour-card coordination, WPS payroll support, records, onboarding, and recruitment coordination across the group's open roles.\n\n**Key responsibilities**\n\n* Coordinate visa, labour card, Emirates ID, and medical processing via PRO/typing centre (Tasheel, MOHRE, GDRFA portals); track expiries and renewals.  \n* Support monthly payroll and WPS submissions; maintain attendance, overtime, and leave records for factory and office staff.  \n* Maintain employee files and HRIS records (Bayzat / ZenHR) \u2014 joiners, transfers, exits, end-of-service/gratuity data.  \n* Run onboarding/offboarding logistics: offer letters, MOHRE contract registration, inductions, asset issue/return.  \n* Coordinate recruitment admin across the group's open roles \u2014 screening logistics, interview scheduling, candidate correspondence, agency liaison.  \n* Handle first-line employee queries; keep HR compliant with UAE Labour Law and MOHRE requirements.\n\n**Must-have**\n\n* 1\u20134 years HR/admin experience in the UAE.  \n* Working knowledge of UAE Labour Law, WPS, and visa/labour-card processes.  \n* HRIS familiarity (Bayzat, ZenHR, or similar) and strong MS Office/Excel.  \n* Fluent English; strong records discipline and confidentiality.\n\n**Nice-to-have**\n\n* Experience in an industrial-sector employer: manufacturing, HVAC, MEP, construction, contracting, facilities management, or building materials (blue-collar / labour-camp workforce exposure).  \n* Arabic language.  \n* CIPD or equivalent HR certification.  \n* Hands-on PRO / government-portal experience (Tasheel, MOHRE, GDRFA).\n\n",
